  "summary": "The source's layout measurements and bit searches reproduce, but its planted-message controls do not establish enough recovery power for a broad negative verdict.",
  "finding": "Five of eleven measured layout features pass the source's two-group screen; none of eight bit-channel searches passes. Yet the strongest planted 64-bit line-fill message recovers only 55/64 bits (85.9%) against a 95% requirement, and a separate source-labeled PASS decodes only 29/77 intended ASCII characters.",
  "limitations": "This is an exact-source, source-known replay of one line detector. The image/canonical line alignment and control failures limit interpretation. No actual payload is recovered; other measurements, encodings or detectors remain open.",
  "next_steps": "Repair image-to-text line alignment and demonstrate full planted-message recovery under a fixed decoder before using a negative scan to exclude a line channel.",
